From 9e0398ddcd28b1f2ea6746cf5313872b0c5220ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:43:40 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Arena: the greeter explains the arena the first time on a new
 save

The first talk with the greeter (ACTOR_GREETER, beside the New Game spawn) shows two
messages of three pages each: cups, the attendant and Solo, the party growing and new Djinn
at the party manager, shops and the next cup, replays, gear rewards, side cups, Multiplayer.
Then she says her stock welcome as before. Once per save: FLAG_ARENA_ONBOARDED, the
reserved persistent byte 0x7e0, set at the end; ArenaBoot_NewGame clears it. The switch is
ARENA_ONBOARDING (arena_config.h, default on). The generated cup messages moved up by two
ids (scripts/gen-cups.py re-run). No automatic walk-up trigger: the talk is enough.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
